## 5. Evaluation Strategy

### 5.1 Metrics to Track

**During Training:**
- Loss (should decrease smoothly)
- Token accuracy (% correct tokens)
- Entropy (model confidence)
- Reward margins (Stage 3 only)

**Post-Training:**
- **Exact Match Accuracy:** Does output exactly match correct code?
- **Top-3 Accuracy:** Is correct code in top 3 predictions?
- **Reasoning Quality:** Are `<think>` traces coherent? (manual review)
- **Code Category Accuracy:** Breakdown by ICD/CPT/HCPCS

### 5.2 Test Sets

**Hold-Out Test Set:** 10% of data, never seen during training

**Test Categories:**
1. **Common Codes:** Frequently used codes (expect >90% accuracy)
2. **Rare Codes:** Less common codes (harder, expect >70% accuracy)
3. **Ambiguous Narratives:** Multiple possible codes (challenging)
4. **Out-of-Distribution:** New phrasing styles

**Success Criteria:**
- Overall accuracy >85%
- Common codes >90%
- Reasoning traces coherent in >95% of cases

